# .security-scan-allowlist — patterns intentionally present in this project.
# Each line is an extended regex; lines matching it (within file CONTENT only,
# not file paths) are skipped by ~/.claude/hooks/lib/security-scan-core.sh.
#
# Keep this list SHORT and JUSTIFIED. Never use a project-name pattern that
# could also substring-match a leaked URL — that's how leaks slip through.

# Project owner appears in GitHub URLs (badges, clone instructions).
github\.com/renefichtmueller/adaptive-llm-gateway

# Documented install paths for the OSS user. The bridge directories named
# here are this project's own deploy targets, not external infrastructure.
/opt/llm-gateway(/|$|")
/opt/(openai|claude|copilot|codex|gemini|m365-copilot|aider)-bridge(/|$|")

# npm scoped package + package.json name field.
@llm-gateway/
"name":[[:space:]]*"llm-gateway

# Comments / log messages referencing the project name without a hostname.
(PM2 entry point|Build-drift guard|deployed to|Deploy(ing)?) for? .*llm-gateway
